  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><sup><strong>Source:</strong> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/533835/diamond-spheres-hustle-bustle?src=newest%3Faffiliate_id%3D3028400\">Diamond Spheres: Hustle &amp; Bustle</a></sup></p>\n<p>You can reveal this plan as an immediate action by revealing that an item that you once possessed is no longer in your possession. You decide when the plan is revealed where the item is actually located—this could be a location you generally frequent (such as a personal abode) or an ally, but you must not have used such an object since you last frequented the area.</p>\n<p>If the item’s actual location is not easily accessible or is intended to be planted on an unaware creature, you must succeed at a Sleight of Hand or Stealth check to successfully plant the object. The DC for this check is usually equal to the Perception check result of the creature (or guardians of the area) as if they had taken 10 on the check (although as normal for a plan, is up to GMs discretion). A relevant disguise may instead require a Disguise check, or even remove the need for a check altogether, up to GM discretion.</p>\n<p>On a failure, the item remains in your possession. If you fail by 5 or more, the relevant creature(s) are aware of the attempt (including the item intended to be planted).</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/subterfuge#toc19\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
      "instructions": ""
    },
